-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Fourth Term Once Commuted Close Mixed
-- statement:
--   **The once-commuted fourth term is within the self-consistency square root of the mixed term.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and assume complete G self consistency at level `zeta`. The once-commuted fourth-term average and the mixed fourth-term average differ by at most one square root of the self-consistency error:
--
--   $$
--   \left|T_{4,\mathrm{once}}-T_{4,\mathrm{mixed}}\right|\le\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The left and right contraction witnesses control the two operator orientations, while the complete-part pair bound supplies the self-consistency comparison. This closes the first square-root `zeta` step before the scalar chain returns to the named once-commuted expression.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateFourthTerm_once_commuted_close_mixed`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
